# Firebase Read Strategy

## Hard Limits (Spark Plan — free)

| Resource | Daily Limit | Resets at midnight Pacific |
|----------|-------------|---------------------------|
| Reads | 50,000/day | Exceeding = shut off until next day |
| Writes | 20,000/day | |
| Deletes | 20,000/day | |
| Storage | 1 GiB | |
| Egress | 10 GiB/month | |

Available for app users: **~50,000 reads/day**

## Firestore Collection

Single active collection: **`article_bundles`**

Each document holds up to 50 articles in an `a` array with short field names (`i,t,d,img,u,p,s,c,tr`).
1 Firestore read = up to 50 articles.

Legacy collections (`news_articles`, `categories`, `rss_metrics`) deleted via one-time `cleanup-firebase.yml` workflow.

## Sync Parameters (SyncManager.kt)

| Parameter | Value | Why |
|-----------|-------|-----|
| `MIN_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS` | 30 sec | Cooldown between fetches — prevents spamming reads |
| `AUTO_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` | 30 min | Matches GitHub Actions schedule — silent, in viewModelScope |

Old constants (`BATCH_SIZE`, `MAX_SYNC_CAP`, `STALE_THRESHOLD_MS`) removed — replaced by `FetchQuotaManager`.

## Quota System (FetchQuotaManager.kt)

| Parameter | Value | Why |
|-----------|-------|-----|
| `DAILY_CAP` | 50 fetches/day | Hard daily limit per device |
| `MONTHLY_CAP` | 1,300 | Rollover bucket for unused daily fetches |
| Time buckets | MORNING(20), AFTERNOON(8), EVENING(12), NIGHT(8), LATE_NIGHT(2) | Distributes fetches across IST time windows |

### Sync Flow (SyncManager.syncNews)

1. Room empty → force fetch (bypass quota), deduct from daily — first install path
2. Last sync < 30 sec → return `SyncResult.COOLDOWN`
3. `canFetch()` true → fetch from Firebase, `recordFetch()` only after successful upsert
4. `canFetch()` false → return `BUCKET_EXHAUSTED` or `QUOTA_EXHAUSTED`

### API Signatures

- `SyncManager.syncNews(trigger: SyncTrigger): Result<SyncResult>`
- `NewsRepository.refreshNews(trigger: SyncTrigger): Result<SyncResult>`
- `SyncTrigger` enum: `APP_OPEN`, `PULL_TO_REFRESH`
- `SyncResult` enum: `SUCCESS`, `COOLDOWN`, `BUCKET_EXHAUSTED`, `QUOTA_EXHAUSTED`, `SKIPPED`

## Deletion Policy (Firebase + Room)

- **Firebase**: Legacy collections deleted via one-time cleanup script. `article_bundles` accumulates indefinitely.
- **Room**: Only `@Upsert`. DAO delete methods exist but have zero callers in the sync flow.
- **Bookmarks**: User can unbookmark (removes from bookmarks table only, not articles).
- **Task F2 (pending)**: Full deletion policy redesign for both Firebase and Room. Not yet designed or approved.
- Until F2 is done, both Firebase (`article_bundles`) and Room accumulate all articles indefinitely.

## Safety Guards

1. **Cooldown** = 30 sec — skip if lastSync < 30s ago, return `SyncResult.COOLDOWN`
2. **Time-bucket quota** — per-IST-window fetch limits (MORNING 20, AFTERNOON 8, EVENING 12, NIGHT 8, LATE_NIGHT 2)
3. **Daily cap** = 50 fetches/day — hard limit, overflow uses monthly rollover bucket
4. **Monthly cap** = 1,300 — unused daily fetches roll over, resets each month
5. **Auto-refresh** = 30 min — silent, foreground only (viewModelScope)
6. **Room-empty bypass** — first install always fetches, deducts from daily quota

*Note: Category sync guard removed — categories are now seeded locally from `LocalCategories.kt`, zero Firebase reads.*

## Read Budget Per User Per Day (bundle system — 1 read = 50 articles)

| User Type | Session | Pulls | Auto-refreshes | Bundle Reads/Day | Approx. Articles |
|-----------|---------|-------|----------------|------------------|------------------|
| Light (15 min) | 15 min | 1 | 0 | ~2 | ~100 |
| Normal (1 hr) | 1 hr | 2 | 1 | ~4 | ~200 |
| Heavy (3-4 hr) | 3 hr | 5 | 5 | ~11 | ~550 |
| Power (8 hr) | 8 hr | 10 | 16 | ~22 | ~1,100 |
| First-time (full) | 30 min | 1 | 0 | ~6 | ~300 |

## DAU Capacity on Free Tier

| Scenario | DAU |
|----------|-----|
| All light | ~25,000 |
| All normal | ~12,500 |
| All heavy | ~4,500 |
| Realistic mix (60% light, 30% normal, 10% heavy) | **~16,000+** |
| Early stage (10-20 users) | <0.1% of limit |

(~48x improvement over single-article reads)

## Zero Firebase Reads Operations

- Browse / scroll → Room PagingSource
- Switch category → Room PagingSource
- Load more (pagination) → Room PagingSource
- Search → Room FTS query
- Category list → Room (seeded locally from `LocalCategories.kt`)

## Rules for Any Code Change

- NEVER add a new Firebase read path without calculating its impact on the daily budget
- NEVER reduce sync cooldown below 30 seconds without recalculating DAU capacity
- NEVER remove or weaken any of the safety guards (cooldown, bucket quota, daily cap, monthly cap)
- NEVER add deletion calls to `article_bundles` until Task F2 (deletion policy redesign) is designed and approved
- Room is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH — UI never reads Firestore directly
- Any new sync feature must show reads/day math before implementation
- NEVER query individual articles from Firebase — always read full bundles
